Haan. AWS EC2 Linux → on-premises Windows Server ke liye rsync use kar sakte ho.
Lekin Windows Server par pehle SSH/SFTP server hona chahiye, kyunki normal Windows rsync setup nahi hota.

500 GB Oracle backup ke case mein flow:

EC2 Ubuntu
   │
   │ rsync over SSH
   ▼
Windows Server
D:\Oracle-Backup

1. Windows Server par OpenSSH Server enable karo

Windows Server mein PowerShell as Administrator:

Get-WindowsCapability -Online | Where-Object Name -like 'OpenSSH.Server*'

Install:

Add-WindowsCapability -Online -Name OpenSSH.Server~~~~0.0.1.0

SSH service start:

Start-Service sshd

Automatic startup:

Set-Service -Name sshd -StartupType Automatic

Check:

Get-Service sshd

2. Windows Firewall mein SSH allow karo

PowerShell Administrator:

New-NetFirewallRule -Name sshd `
    -DisplayName "OpenSSH Server (sshd)" `
    -Enabled True `
    -Direction Inbound `
    -Protocol TCP `
    -Action Allow `
    -LocalPort 22

Security: Agar Windows Server Internet par exposed hai, port 22 ko 0.0.0.0/0 se open mat karo. EC2 ke known public IP ya, 
better, VPN/private network se restrict karo.
3. Windows Server par backup folder banao

Example:

New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path "D:\Oracle-Backup"

Suppose Windows username:

backupuser

4. EC2 se Windows Server connectivity test karo

EC2 Ubuntu par:

ssh backupuser@WINDOWS_SERVER_IP

Example:

ssh backupuser@203.0.113.20

Agar login ho gaya, to rsync configure karna easy hai.
5. EC2 par rsync install karo

Ubuntu:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install rsync -y

Check:

rsync --version

6. Rsync command

Maan lo EC2 par Oracle backup:

/backup/oracle/

Windows Server par destination:

D:\Oracle-Backup\

Rsync command:

rsync -avh --progress /backup/oracle/ backupuser@203.0.113.20:/D:/Oracle-Backup/

Windows OpenSSH ke path handling mein environment ke hisaab se path syntax vary kar sakta hai. Agar /D:/Oracle-Backup/ 
work na kare, Windows SSH session mein check karo:

ssh backupuser@203.0.113.20

aur:

pwd

ya Windows OpenSSH ke configured home/path ke according destination use karo.
7. 500 GB ke liye important rsync options

Aap Oracle RMAN backup transfer kar rahe ho to:

rsync -avh --progress --partial \
  /backup/oracle/ \
  backupuser@203.0.113.20:/D:/Oracle-Backup/

--partial ka fayda:

500 GB transfer
       ↓
300 GB transferred
       ↓
Network disconnect
       ↓
rsync again
       ↓
existing partial data se continue

Har baar zero se start karne ki zarurat nahi padti.
Agar network slow hai

Compression use kar sakte ho:

rsync -avh --progress --partial -z \
  /backup/oracle/ \
  backupuser@203.0.113.20:/D:/Oracle-Backup/

Lekin Oracle RMAN backup files aksar already compressed/encrypted ho sakti hain, isliye -z CPU/network trade-off ke hisaab se test karna chahiye.
8. SSH key use karna better hai

Password ke bajay EC2 par SSH key generate:

ssh-keygen -t ed25519

Phir public key:

cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub

Windows Server ke user ke SSH authorized keys mein public key configure karo.

Uske baad:

rsync -avh --progress --partial \
  -e "ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519" \
  /backup/oracle/ \
  backupuser@203.0.113.20:/D:/Oracle-Backup/

Isse .pem ki zarurat nahi hai. Ye key specifically EC2 → Windows authentication ke liye hai.
9. Oracle RMAN backup ke saath

Aapke 500 GB Oracle database ke liye main ye workflow rakhunga:

             EC2 Ubuntu
                 │
                 ▼
          Oracle Database
                 │
                 ▼
            RMAN Backup
                 │
                 ▼
          /backup/oracle/
                 │
                 │ rsync + SSH
                 ▼
       ┌────────────────────┐
       │ Windows Server     │
       │ D:\Oracle-Backup\  │
       └────────────────────┘

Database ke live datafiles ko directly rsync mat karo. Oracle database ka consistent backup RMAN se banao, 
phir RMAN backup pieces ko rsync karo.
Daily automation

Example:

rsync -avh --progress --partial \
  /backup/oracle/ \
  backupuser@203.0.113.20:/D:/Oracle-Backup/

Is command ko RMAN backup complete hone ke baad cron/script se run kara sakte ho.

Agar aap 500 GB Oracle DB + EC2 Ubuntu + Windows Server use kar rahe ho, to main next step mein aapko ek complete production-style script de sakta hoon jo:

RMAN backup → rsync → interrupted transfer resume → log → 7/30-day retention → cron
