Haan, agar Amazon RDS for Oracle hai, to aap RDS ke andar directly OS-level rman/expdp command jaise EC2 par normally nahi chala sakte. RDS managed service hai aur OS access/SYSDBA privileges restricted hain.

Agar goal hai:

    RDS Oracle → backup/export → On-Prem Windows Server ya GCP VM

to do alag requirements hain.
1. Agar complete RDS recovery backup chahiye

RDS ke automated backups / manual snapshots use karo:

RDS Oracle
   │
   └── RDS Snapshot / Automated Backup
             │
             ▼
        AWS Recovery

Ye backup AWS ke andar RDS restore/recovery ke liye hai. Isko simply .bkp file bana kar Windows/GCP VM par download nahi kar sakte. RDS backup/snapshot management AWS ke through hota hai.

2. Agar database ka actual backup/export file chahiye

Yahan Oracle Data Pump (expdp) use karna appropriate hai.

Architecture:

             AWS
┌─────────────────────────┐
│ RDS for Oracle          │
│                         │
│ Oracle Data Pump        │
└───────────┬─────────────┘
            │
            │ .dmp files
            ▼
        Amazon S3
            │
       ┌────┴─────┐
       │          │
       ▼          ▼
   Windows       GCP VM
   Server        Oracle VM

AWS officially RDS for Oracle se Data Pump export ko support karta hai. RDS Oracle ke S3 integration ke through DATA_PUMP_DIR 
se files S3 mein upload ki ja sakti hain.

Example workflow

RDS Oracle par Data Pump export:

BEGIN
  DBMS_DATAPUMP...
END;
/

Ya Oracle Data Pump utilities expdp/impdp ko remote host/Oracle Client se use kiya ja sakta hai. AWS documentation 
RDS Oracle se on-premises ya EC2 Oracle database ke liye Data Pump movement ko explicitly support karti hai.

Uske baad RDS Oracle ke S3 integration se:

SELECT rdsadmin.rdsadmin_s3_tasks.upload_to_s3(
    p_bucket_name    => 'my-oracle-backup-bucket',
    p_directory_name => 'DATA_PUMP_DIR'
) AS task_id
FROM dual;

AWS documentation mein isi mechanism se DATA_PUMP_DIR ki files S3 par upload karne ka example diya gaya hai.

Phir Windows Server ya GCP VM se:

aws s3 cp s3://my-oracle-backup-bucket/ ./oracle-backup/ --recursive

Aur agar destination par Oracle database hai, to:

impdp ...

se restore/import kar sakte ho.
3. Agar S3 mein permanently nahi rakhna

Aapka flow temporary S3 ke through bhi ho sakta hai:

RDS Oracle
    │
    │ Data Pump
    ▼
S3
    │
    │ aws s3 cp
    ▼
Windows Server / GCP VM
    │
    ▼
Oracle Database

S3 ko transfer/staging location ki tarah use kar sakte ho. RDS Oracle aur S3 integration ke liye bucket same AWS Region mein hona chahiye.

500 GB database ke liye

500 GB ke liye main ye architecture rakhunga:

                 RDS Oracle
                     │
          ┌──────────┴──────────┐
          │                     │
     RDS Automated          Data Pump
       Backup/Snapshot          │
          │                     ▼
          │                    S3
          │                     │
          ▼                     │
    AWS Recovery                │
                                ▼
                       On-Prem / GCP VM

RDS Snapshot = AWS-side disaster recovery.

Data Pump dump (.dmp) = database data ko AWS ke bahar Oracle environment mein le jaane/restore karne ke liye.

Aur 500 GB ke case mein Data Pump ko parallel workers/dump files mein split karna performance aur transfer management 
ke liye useful ho sakta hai. AWS bhi large Data Pump exports ke liye multiple dump files/parallel option
ka documentation deta hai.

